<article class="env-corollary" id="05FK">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05FK">Corollary <span data-tag="05FK">8.5.1.15</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $n$ be an integer. Then the collection of $n$-truncated objects of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is closed under retracts. Similarly, the collection of $n$-truncated morphisms of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is closed under retracts in $\operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollary <a data-tag="05E6" href="/tag/05E6">8.5.1.12</a> with Remark <a data-tag="05EM" href="/tag/05EM">7.1.3.13</a> and Proposition <a data-tag="06TF" href="/tag/06TF">7.1.3.15</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
